"comparison": "Both Intel and Micron disclose obligations to purchase minimum quantities of goods or services with remaining terms exceeding one year, though the specific nature and structure differ. Intel's obligation is tied to a specific semiconductor co-investment program (Ireland SCIP) for Fab 34 output, triggering volume-related damages if minimums are not met, with obligations starting upon construction completion or Q3 2027. In contrast, Micron discloses a broader portfolio of noncancelable purchase obligations totaling approximately $6.7 billion, which include payments for goods, services, and property, plant, and equipment with fixed or minimum quantities and prices, scheduled over a multi-year horizon (2025-2030+).",
